Vendored support files, so that terps/scarier is self-contained
===============================================================

Gargoyle takes Scarier as a drop-in copy of this whole directory (see the
scarier block in gargoyle's terps/CMakeLists.txt).  Anything the engine needs
that lives outside terps/scarier in the Spatterlight tree therefore has to have
a copy in here, or the copied folder will not build.

  randomness.c
  randomness.h   Verbatim copies of terps/common_utils/randomness.[ch], the
                 shared seedable erkyrath RNG, which both engines draw
                 from.  The engine includes THIS randomness.h in every build
                 ("common_utils/randomness.h", no include path needed), but
                 the Spatterlight app and the Makefiles compile the original
                 randomness.c; the copy of that is compiled only by
                 out-of-tree builds.  Keep them byte-identical:
                 `make -f Makefile.headless vendorcheck`, part of the default
                 `test` target, fails if they drift.

  rgbsurface.h   Verbatim copy of terps/common_utils/rgbsurface.h, the shared
                 software rasteriser (header-only) behind the map pane; the
                 Quest 5 grid map in terps/question uses the original.  Unlike
                 randomness, Scarier includes THIS copy in every build
                 (mapdraw.h: "common_utils/rgbsurface.h"), which needs no
                 include path.  Keep it byte-identical to the original:
                 vendorcheck covers it too.

  sc_garglk.c
  sc_garglk.h    Portability for the ADRIFT 5 engine.  strndup() for
                 toolchains without one -- MinGW and MSVC, where Gargoyle's
                 CMake probe defines GARGLK_NEEDS_STRNDUP; sc_garglk.c is an
                 empty translation unit everywhere else, and no part of the
                 Spatterlight build.  And strcasecmp()/strncasecmp(): the
                 header includes <strings.h>, or under MSVC, which has no
                 such header, maps them to _stricmp()/_strnicmp().  Included
                 by every adrift5/ file that compares case-insensitively,
                 instead of <strings.h>.

Fixes made here in the Gargoyle tree belong upstream in the Spatterlight tree
first; the copy only ever travels one way.
